      "Language": "hun",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "INTRODUCTION AND AIM",
          "content": "Coronary computer tomography angiography is a unique non-invasive imaging technique with the capability to provide information regarding plaque quantity, burden and structure. A reliable registry is required to use the data of these examinations in research projects. The difficulty is that registries need double data entry simultaneously to the hospital information system."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "Our registry solves this problem through a structured reporting tool, which generates clinical report and stores all data simultaneously. The automatically generated report is based on international guidelines."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Between August 1. 2014 and September 1. 2015 we registered the data of 2866 patients. Coronary plaque was observed in 77.03% of the patients, 33.18% of the plaques were calcified. Severe stenosis was present in 13.71% of the patients."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The structured reporting decreases reporting time, eliminates double data entry related errors. Our goal is to initiate a nationwide, unified registry, the National Plaque Registry and Database. Orv. Hetil., 2017, 158(3), 106-110."
        }
      ]},
